# Styling & Theme Guidelines

## Tailwind CSS v4 Configuration
The project uses Tailwind CSS v4 with the new `@theme inline` directive in [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css).

## Cyberpunk Theme System
The project implements a complete cyberpunk theme with OKLCH color space for consistent theming.

### Color System
Use the predefined color variables from the theme:

```css
/* Primary Colors */
--color-primary: oklch(0.7 0.15 280); /* Electric purple */
--color-primary-foreground: oklch(0.98 0.02 220);

/* Secondary Colors */
--color-secondary: oklch(0.9 0.05 220);
--color-secondary-foreground: oklch(0.2 0.05 220);

/* Accent Colors */
--color-accent: oklch(0.6 0.2 160); /* Neon green */
--color-accent-foreground: oklch(0.98 0.02 220);

/* Background Colors */
--color-background: oklch(0.96 0.02 220); /* Light mode */
--color-foreground: oklch(0.1 0.02 220);
```

### Dark Mode Support
The theme includes comprehensive dark mode variants:

```css
.dark {
  --color-background: oklch(0.05 0.02 220); /* Dark backgrounds */
  --color-foreground: oklch(0.95 0.02 220);
  --color-primary: oklch(0.8 0.2 280); /* Brighter purple in dark */
}
```

## Tailwind Class Usage

### Container and Layout
```tsx
<section className="container mx-auto px-4 py-16 relative z-10">
  <div className="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center space-y-6">
    {/* Content */}
  </div>
</section>
```

### Typography
```tsx
<h1 className="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-6xl">
  Main Heading
</h1>
<p className="text-xl text-muted-foreground">
  Subtitle text
</p>
```

### Button Styling
```tsx
<Button size="lg" variant="outline" className="hover:bg-primary/10">
  Button Text
</Button>
```

### Card Components
```tsx
<Card className="border-2 border-primary/20 hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle>Card Title</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>
    Card content
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

## Custom CSS Effects
The theme includes custom cyberpunk effects:

### Neon Glow Effects
```css
.neon-glow {
  box-shadow: 
    0 0 5px var(--color-primary),
    0 0 10px var(--color-primary),
    0 0 15px var(--color-primary);
}

.neon-text {
  text-shadow: 
    0 0 5px var(--color-primary),
    0 0 10px var(--color-primary);
}
```

### Animated Borders
```css
.animated-border {
  position: relative;
  background: linear-gradient(45deg, 
    var(--color-primary), 
    var(--color-accent), 
    var(--color-primary)
  );
  background-size: 200% 200%;
  animation: gradient-shift 3s ease infinite;
}
```

## Responsive Design
Always use responsive classes:

```tsx
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:justify-center">
  <div className="w-full sm:w-auto">
    Content
  </div>
</div>
```

## Theme Toggle Integration
The project includes a [ThemeToggle](mdc:src/components/ThemeToggle.tsx) component that:
- Switches between light and dark modes
- Persists preference in localStorage
- Uses the `dark` class on the root element

## Color Accessibility
- Maintain WCAG AA contrast ratios
- Test both light and dark modes
- Use semantic color names (primary, secondary, accent)
- Avoid hardcoded color values

## Animation Integration
Combine Tailwind classes with Framer Motion:

```tsx
<motion.div
  className="bg-card border border-border rounded-lg p-6"
  whileHover={{ 
    scale: 1.02,
    boxShadow: "0 0 20px var(--color-primary)"
  }}
  transition={{ duration: 0.2 }}
>
  Content
</motion.div>
```